// aug20a epoch_refire (ryouko1, campaign-minimized): `m` is read only by
// the guard of a STRUCTURE-FAILED arm, so its deliveries re-derive the
// tail chain f(3)->f(0) every cycle without being a consumed input. On
// each re-derivation pass the `0 =>` arm is re-woken (it slept on the
// n=3 pass — loop plumbing, no trigger). The arm-body region's DynCall
// slot was slept with the arm, and sleep RESET its first-dispatch
// flag, so the next dispatch forced the init view and delivered every
// arg fired — inside a quiet frame, where the interp's constants stay
// on the value channel and a re-woken call site is resumed, not
// re-primed. Interp [0:true]; JIT re-fired on every `m` delivery.
{let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2, i64:3, i64:4]); let m = x; let rec f = |n| select n {i64:0 => select i64:9223372036854775807 {i64:0 if m == i64:0 => i64:1, _ => math::abs(f64:-3.5) == f64:3.5}, _ => f(i64:0)}; f(i64:3)}
